   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving access to HIV prevention, treatment, and care services for key populations in Russia - Russian Federation (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Russian Federation, HIV, Open Health Institute (OHI)This program has the following goals: Assistance in developing and strengthening of the national legal, methodological and financial base to provide sustainability and broad coverage of the key groups with services on HIV prevention, treatment, care and support. The objectives of this program are: Strengthening of advocacy to remove legal barriers to treatment and to apply scientifically based preventive programs to the national HIV strategy and existing health care and social safety system.  Strengthening of community systems to influence service and advocative activities on HIV prevention among vulnerable group.  Support of prevention programs to maintain the level of HIV prevalence among IDUs and their partners in the selected regions.  Support of prevention programs to maintain the level of HIV prevalence among MSM in the selected regions.  Support of prevention programs to maintain the level of HIV prevalence among sex-workers in the selected regions</narrative>
  </description>
